          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mrwoi7cj5icvj99e",
          "message": {
            "text": "The user-visible half of HS-9380: the banner said \"N **Claude** connections active — triggers route to the oldest one\" regardless of `ai_tool`. Split by transport because the semantics genuinely differ: on `claude-channel` the FIFO-leader routing claim and the `/mcp` reconnect hint are true; on spawn drives (mcp-hooks/acp) every trigger launches a fresh run (its MCP child is tagged `drive` and excluded from this count), so neither claim applies. Kept pure/no-DOM so the wording is pinned by `multiConnectionWarning.test.ts`.\n",
            "markdown": "The user-visible half of HS-9380: the banner said \"N **Claude** connections active — triggers route to the oldest one\" regardless of `ai_tool`. Split by transport because the semantics genuinely differ: on `claude-channel` the FIFO-leader routing claim and the `/mcp` reconnect hint are true; on spawn drives (mcp-hooks/acp) every trigger launches a fresh run (its MCP child is tagged `drive` and excluded from this count), so neither claim applies. Kept pure/no-DOM so the wording is pinned by `multiConnectionWarning.test.ts`.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/multiConnectionWarning.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 22,
                  "endLine": 43,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function multiConnectionMessages(aiTool: string | undefined): MultiConnectionMessages {\n  const agent = agentDisplayName(aiTool);\n  if (deriveDefaultTransport(aiTool) === 'claude-channel') {\n    // Claude-channel transport: triggers really do route to the FIFO leader, and\n    // `/mcp` in the wanted Claude is the reconnect path.\n    return {\n      warning: (count) => `${String(count)} ${agent} connections active — triggers route to the oldest one. Disconnect all, then /mcp to reconnect the one you want.`,\n      disconnectedToast: (killed) => `Disconnected ${String(killed)} ${agent} connection${killed === 1 ? '' : 's'} — run /mcp in the ${agent} you want to use to reconnect`,\n      noneToast: `No ${agent} connections to disconnect`,\n    };\n  }\n  // Spawn-drive transports (mcp-hooks / acp): the play button launches a fresh\n  // one-shot run each time (its own MCP connection is tagged `drive` and not\n  // counted here), so >1 mains = extra interactive agent sessions holding a Hot\n  // Sheet MCP connection. No trigger misrouting, and `/mcp` is Claude-specific —\n  // drop both claims.\n  return {\n    warning: (count) => `${String(count)} ${agent} sessions hold a Hot Sheet connection for this project. Play runs are unaffected; Disconnect all to clear stale sessions.`,\n    disconnectedToast: (killed) => `Disconnected ${String(killed)} ${agent} connection${killed === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,\n    noneToast: `No ${agent} connections to disconnect`,\n  };\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
